# Applications Page Structure and APIs

## Page Overview
Main application tracking page: [applications/page.tsx](mdc:medshadow/src/app/applications/page.tsx)

## Key Components
1. Application Status Tracking
   - Status badges (pending, reviewing, accepted, rejected, onboarding)
   - Timeline view of application progress
   - Color-coded status indicators

2. Next Steps Section
   - Checklist of required documents/tasks
   - Due dates and completion tracking
   - Document upload functionality

3. Notifications/Updates
   - Color-coded by type (info, success, warning, error)
   - Chronological timeline
   - Read/unread status tracking

## Required APIs

1. `/api/applications`
   - GET: List all applications for current user
   - Query params: status, page, limit
   - Returns: Paginated list of applications with related opportunity data

2. `/api/applications/[id]`
   - GET: Fetch specific application details
   - PUT: Update application status
   - Required fields: status, nextSteps, notifications

3. `/api/applications/[id]/documents`
   - POST: Upload required documents
   - GET: List uploaded documents
   - Required: Document validation and storage

4. `/api/applications/[id]/tasks`
   - PUT: Update task completion status
   - Required fields: taskId, completed, completionDate

5. `/api/applications/notifications`
   - GET: Fetch all notifications
   - PUT: Mark notifications as read
   - Query params: read, type, page, limit

## Data Models

```typescript
interface Application {
  _id: string;
  opportunity: Opportunity;
  status: 'pending' | 'reviewing' | 'accepted' | 'rejected' | 'onboarding';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
  nextSteps?: {
    type: 'document' | 'form' | 'task' | 'meeting';
    title: string;
    description: string;
    deadline?: string;
    completed?: boolean;
  }[];
  notifications?: {
    _id: string;
    message: string;
    date: string;
    read: boolean;
    type: 'info' | 'success' | 'warning' | 'error';
  }[];
}
```

## Implementation Notes
- Real-time updates using WebSocket for status changes
- Document storage in cloud storage (AWS S3/Firebase)
- Notification system should support email notifications
- All API endpoints require authentication
- Rate limiting for document uploads and API calls
